From: Scrumpper <190908034+Scrumpper@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 22:35:36 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 24/59] PCI: rockchip: dw: program PTM only when the DT routes
 a ptm interrupt

rk_pcie_host_config() runs at probe and on every resume, including each
bcmdhd ROCKCHIP_PCIE_PM_CTRL_RESET. Since the rk3572 import it writes
the PTM responder local clock (DBI 0x290/0x28c/0x284) and enables and
unmasks the PTM context IRQs (client APB 0x488/0x484) on every SoC. Only
rk3572.dtsi names a "ptm" interrupt; on rk3588 no handler is ever
registered and probe logs "IRQ ptm not found". The 6.1 driver has no
PTM code at all.

Record whether interrupt-names carries "ptm" at resource time and skip
the PTM block and the PTM IRQ request otherwise. rk3588 returns to 6.1
behaviour; rk3572 unchanged. 6.12 t6.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01P6itje71iKPFBX7YKkfvRo
---
 drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-dw-rockchip.c | 12 +++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-dw-rockchip.c b/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-dw-rockchip.c
index 163724e66..1257c3ae0 100644
--- a/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-dw-rockchip.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-dw-rockchip.c
@@ -166,6 +166,7 @@ struct rk_pcie {
 	bool				is_lpbk;
 	bool				is_comp;
 	bool				probe_ok;
+	bool				has_ptm;
 	struct completion		probe_done;
 	bool				keep_power_in_suspend;
 	struct regulator		*vpcie3v3;
@@ -906,6 +907,10 @@ static int rk_pcie_resource_get(struct platform_device *pdev,
 	if (device_property_read_bool(&pdev->dev, "rockchip,skip-scan-in-resume"))
 		rk_pcie->skip_scan_in_resume = true;
 
+	/* PTM only on SoCs that route a ptm interrupt */
+	rk_pcie->has_ptm = of_property_match_string(pdev->dev.of_node,
+						    "interrupt-names", "ptm") >= 0;
+
 	/* Force into loopback master mode */
 	if (device_property_read_bool(&pdev->dev, "rockchip,lpbk-master")) {
 		rk_pcie->is_lpbk = true;
@@ -1090,7 +1095,9 @@ static int rk_pcie_request_sys_irq(struct rk_pcie *rk_pcie,
 		return ret;
 	}
 
-	/* Optional ptm irq */
+	if (!rk_pcie->has_ptm)
+		return 0;
+
 	irq = platform_get_irq_byname(pdev, "ptm");
 	if (irq < 0)
 		return 0;
@@ -1826,6 +1833,9 @@ static int rk_pcie_host_config(struct rk_pcie *rk_pcie)
 	dw_pcie_writel_dbi2(pci, PCI_BASE_ADDRESS_0, 0x0);
 	dw_pcie_writel_dbi2(pci, PCI_BASE_ADDRESS_1, 0x0);
 
+	if (!rk_pcie->has_ptm)
+		return 0;
+
 	/*
 	 * Program PTM responder local clock with 64-bit nanosecond timestamp.
 	 *
